# --- Research data and large local artifacts (moved out in the v3 split) ---
#
# This repository holds code only. Research data moved to a sibling store,
# `../BDA-data` by default; override with BDA_DATA_ROOT. Large local-only
# artifacts (model checkpoints, database dumps) live in `../BDA-local` and are
# never versioned anywhere. See docs/refactor/REPO_SPLIT.md.
#
# The paths below stay ignored so a stale copy in an old working tree — or a
# restore from backup into the old location — cannot be committed by accident.
backups/
models/
deliverables/
fig/
/research projects/

# Consequence worth knowing: tracked files under docs/ and backend_v2/scripts/
# cite paths inside the research store (e.g. "research projects/MANUKA/..."),
# naming evidence a reader cannot obtain from a clone alone. That is deliberate
# — the alternative is committing the bundles — but any conclusion that has to
# survive review on its own should be restated in the doc rather than only cited.
# Scripts that *read* this data must resolve it through
# backend_v2/scripts/_data_root.py, never a hardcoded repo-relative path.

*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
backend_v2/scripts/host-worker.env

# Browser vertical-slice run output (screenshots, traces, per-case failure JSON).
# Regenerated by `npm run test:browser`; never a reviewable artifact.
.superpowers/sdd/*/browser-artifacts/
